- Spot the duplicates: sets of two or more rows that record the same defect at the same site (a sibling, the same mechanism at another site, is not a duplicate). Start from the 7 groups of section 3.2 and add any others the heads suggest, reading the rows whole where the heads leave it unsure. For each set name the row that keeps the content (usually the earlier one, but the one that holds more wins). A set lies inside one group. The rewriter of that group reads the rows whole, confirms the set and closes the duplicates.
